<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Gekko gecko Turing wavenumber at 242 µm (Holocene, Pass 1) (Gekko gecko (Tokay gecko))",
        "Gekko gecko Turing wavenumber at 242 µm (Holocene, Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Gekko gecko (Tokay gecko) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/gekko_gecko_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gekko gecko (Tokay gecko) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/gekko_gecko_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Gekko gecko (Tokay gecko)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Tokay chromatophores implement the Timon scale automaton.",
        "does_not_claim: That adult Tokay ocelli are 242 µm apart.",
        "does_not_claim: That setal adhesion spacing is this pigment wavelength.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Periodic 1936 µm × 1452 µm patch, seed 3235, 12-frame growth GIF.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg field with (a, b) = (0.137, 0.863) and diffusion ratio 1.35 times critical, calibrated so k_c = argmax sigma(k) gives 242 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Manukyan 2017 and Fofonjka 2021: reptile skin can carry a mesoscopic reaction-diffusion pattern (Timon, not Gekko).",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981 use of that wavelength as a coat pre-pattern.",
        "reported_in_source: Saenko 2013: gekkotan color colocalizes structural and pigment cells (Phelsuma, not Gekko).",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system.",
        "transfer_boundary: 242 µm is the slot's primordium detail scale, not a published caliper measurement on Gekko gecko.",
        "transfer_boundary: The Dupont photograph has no scale bar; it constrains pattern class only." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Gekko gecko" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Amphibia & Reptilia (Ootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Gekko" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/gekko_gecko_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; output: docs/media/gekko_gecko_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Gekko gecko (Tokay gecko); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Murray 1981 use of that wavelength as a coat pre-pattern. | Manukyan 2017 and Fofonjka 2021: reptile skin can carry a mesoscopic reaction-diffusion pattern (Timon, not Gekko). | Saenko 2013: gekkotan color colocalizes structural and pigment cells (Phelsuma, not Gekko).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg field with (a, b) = (0.137, 0.863) and diffusion ratio 1.35 times critical, calibrated so k_c = argmax sigma(k) gives 242 µm. | Periodic 1936 µm × 1452 µm patch, seed 3235, 12-frame growth GIF.; transfer_boundary: 242 µm is the slot's primordium detail scale, not a published caliper measurement on Gekko gecko. | The Dupont photograph has no scale bar; it constrains pattern class only.; does_not_claim: That adult Tokay ocelli are 242 µm apart. | That Tokay chromatophores implement the Timon scale automaton. | That setal adhesion spacing is this pigment wavelength.]; other sources: Tokay Gecko (Gekko gecko), Wanree Resort, Pak Chong, Thailand <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tokay_Gecko_(Gekko_gecko)_(7109782823).jpg>; phenomenon_size: 200 µm (0.0002 m, log10=-3.699 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 200 µm to 57.6 cm): 200 µm:gekko-gecko-bioelectric-polarity, 712 µm:gekko-gecko-vertex-packing, 1.3 cm:gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength, 2.4 cm:gekko-gecko-clock-wavefront, 4.2 cm:gekko-gecko-morphogen-condensation, 5.4 cm:gekko-gecko-flux-canalization, 5.9 cm:gekko-gecko-elastic-buckling, 6.9 cm:gekko-gecko-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature22031>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-021-22525-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/1741-7007-11-105> ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-gekko-gecko-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
